 "title": "ApexFold multi-solvent circular dichroism (CD) dataset",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/20616716",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20616716",
 "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">This record contains the circular-dichroism data underlying the study <em>\"Predicting how peptides fold with ApexFold\"</em> (Torres, Cao &amp; de la Fuente-Nunez). The dataset characterises the solvent-dependent secondary structure of short peptides (8&ndash;50 residues) measured across four chemical environments: water, methanol/water, trifluoroethanol/water (3:2, v/v), and SDS micelles (10 mmol/L).&nbsp;CD spectra were acquired on a Jasco J-1500 spectropolarimeter at 50 &micro;mol/L, 25 &deg;C, over 190&ndash;260 nm (1.0 mm path length, three averaged accumulations per condition),</p>",
